laurel 2872: display off keeps the panel awake; the wake shows a frame and checks the panel. Boot 19:34 (2871): the owner locked the phone and the screen never came back: iOS and the kernel alive, swaps and touches go on, every 0x11/0x29 done, panel holds DBV 2047, display on bit set. 2871's self-check found that only the TPG FIFO answers and chose it for writes too, so boot 19:34 is the first boot where 0x28/0x10 reached the panel: the memory DMA answered no read and left 0x54 at 0x28 after 53 20, all earlier boots had no effect from any DCS write and always woke. First real sleep at 19:42:55 changed the panel's power mode from 0x9f to 0x9d for good. 0x11 + 0x29 with the video stream running is a sequence Linux never sends: the DT has lp11-init, a reset sequence and a full on-command set with vendor registers, sent before the video starts. Fix: display off = fade to DBV 0 + black kernel frame, no 0x28/0x10 (the same dark as before, the power of all earlier boots). The wake sends nothing unless a check finds the panel off: one DCS 0x0A after each display on, light still out (bits 7, 4, 3, 2 = 0x9c), mismatch = 0x11, 120 ms, 0x29, 0x53 0x20 once, one more read, one line. Reads after the start: only this one; the settled-value read-back and the way moves are gone (the start self-check keeps the transport and the way). Reads cannot be proven safe in video mode from a log; a wake check runs with the light out. laurelbl_read=0 now means no reads at all, FIFO for writes. Display on with no new iOS frame: fPending is not the last frame on the direct path (stale record, or black until iOS draws): the first tick shows the last direct frame again when the panel still has the black one and nothing waits (its surface is still held by fShowHold). Lines: `LAUREL PANEL: on: ...` after USB is up, `LAUREL PANEL: wake N: panel power 0x.. (start 0x..)` (first 8, then on a change), `LAUREL PANEL: display on, no new iOS frame yet: the last one again (N)` (first 8). The lines `SWEET FB: panel display off, sleep in` and `panel sleep out, display on` are gone. Kill switches: laurelbl_read=0, sweetfb_stayon=1 (existing).

